# Release proposal: Pantry 7.0 — Weekly Planner redesign

Owner: growth-web · Ship: Tue 2026-11-03, 100% of web users · Figma: "Planner 7 final" · Epic: PAN-2207

## Summary

The weekly planner page is rebuilt around day cards. Goals from the brief: less visual clutter on recipe cards, clearer "this week at a glance", and a persistent bottom action bar on mobile.

## Product usage data (from brief, Sept 2026)

- Most frequent planner action: adding a planned recipe's ingredients to the shopping list (avg 9.4 times/week per weekly-active user).
- Second: swapping a recipe for another (2.1 times/week).
- 64% of shopping-list additions happen on mobile.

## What changes

- Each day is a `.day-card` with up to 3 recipe tiles (breakfast/lunch/dinner).
- Recipe tiles show image, title, time and a "Swap" button. The old tile-level "+ List" button is removed to declutter tiles.
- To add a recipe to the shopping list: tap the tile → recipe page → "Ingredients" tab → choose servings in the servings sheet → "Add to list" → toast with "Undo".
- New sticky bottom bar on mobile with "Generate shopping list" (adds all planned recipes for the week) and "Share plan".
- Drag a recipe tile between days to move it. Keyboard and screen-reader users get "Move to…" in each tile's overflow menu.
- Tile images use `loading="lazy"` with explicit `width`/`height` so layout does not shift while scrolling.

## Markup (`planner.html`, abbreviated)

```html
<main class="planner">
  <h1>This week</h1>
  <section class="day-card" aria-labelledby="d-mon">
    <h2 id="d-mon">Monday</h2>
    <ul class="tiles">
      <li class="tile">
        <img src="/img/r/8812-320.webp" width="320" height="200" loading="lazy" alt="">
        <h3>Sheet-pan gnocchi</h3>
        <p class="meta">25 min</p>
        <button class="btn-ghost">Swap</button>
        <button class="btn-icon" aria-label="More options for Sheet-pan gnocchi">⋯</button>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <!-- Tuesday … Sunday follow; Sunday is the last child of .planner -->
</main>
<nav class="action-bar">
  <button class="btn-primary">Generate shopping list</button>
  <button class="btn-ghost">Share plan</button>
</nav>
```

## Styles (`planner.css`)

```css
:root {
  --text: #1d1d1f;
  --muted: #6e6e73;
  --surface: #ffffff;
  --page: #f5f5f7;
  --brand: #0b7a5a;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root {
    --text: #f2f2f7;
    --muted: #a1a1a6;
    --surface: #1c1c1e;
    --page: #000000;
  }
}
body { background: var(--page); color: var(--text); margin: 0; }
.planner { max-width: 960px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 16px; display: grid; gap: 16px; }
.day-card {
  background: #ffffff;
  color: var(--text);
  border-radius: 16px;
  padding: 16px;
  box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.08);
}
.tile .meta { color: var(--muted); }
.action-bar {
  position: fixed; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
  height: 72px; padding: 12px 16px;
  display: flex; gap: 12px;
  background: var(--surface);
  border-top: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08);
}
@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .action-bar { position: static; height: auto; max-width: 960px; margin: 0 auto; }
}
.btn-primary { background: var(--brand); color: #fff; min-height: 48px; border-radius: 12px; }
```

## QA report summary

- Visual QA vs Figma: Chrome 1440px (light), Safari iPhone 14 (light) — pass, pixel diffs < 1%.
- Drag-and-drop between days, "Move to…" menu with keyboard (Tab/Enter/Arrow) and VoiceOver: pass.
- Lighthouse mobile: performance 91, accessibility 100, CLS 0.01.
- Shopping list add via recipe page + undo: pass.

## Rollout

- Ship to 100% Tue 10:00 PT behind `planner_v7`; old planner remains available by flipping the flag off (same API, no data migration).
- Watch: planner page JS errors, shopping-list additions/WAU, planner bounce rate.
